            "block_order": null
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "of the corners, (4) reduce the required thickness and/or reinforcement in the floor slab (moment capacity of the floor slab extension must be developed by bearing on the subgrade) and (5) eliminate the need to anchor the reinforcement by bending at the corners which would ordinarily hinder the placement of the concrete.\n",
            "block_bbox": [
                133,
                267,
                1046,
                369
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "End cells of multi-cubicle arrangements also require the addition of tension reinforcement to resist unbalanced blast loads acting on the end walls. The interior cells do not require this additional reinforcement since the mass and base friction of adjoining cells provide the restraint to resist the lateral forces.",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                391,
                1001,
                495
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Construction details for single cells and end cells of multi-cubicle arrangements are provided in Section 4-68.\n",
